  "query_preview": "..(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 435 AM EDT SUN OCT 18 2026\n\nThe models remain in good agreement through the end of the\nupcoming work week. A ridge will sharpen up in the mid and upper\nlevels over the central CONUS. This will lead to a prolonged\nperiod of dry weather across the Ohio and Tennesseee valleys. The\nmodel agreement decreases a bit more by next weekend, as the\nconfidence lowers regarding the evolution of eastern Pacific \nas it ejects east of the Rockies.\n\nEastern Kentucky will be under the influence of the ridge through\nthe period. Surface high pressure will mainly center to our north\nand northeast through Friday, allowing for only a slow moderation\nin temperatures. Skies will remain mostly clear through next week.\nPatchy frost will continue to be possible in the normally colder\nsheltered valleys once again Monday and Tuesday night, as drier \nlow level air will likely mix down below the blended guidance \nduring peak mixing. Highs will average in the upper 60s and lower \n70s each day, with lows gradually warming through the 30s and \neventually into the 40s each night.",
